authors:
  - name: "cyber-audit-lab"
abstract: >-
  Aggregate results of an exploratory study of the names that 52 language models from nine families (including
  GPT-2 as a pre-chat comparison) choose when asked to name themselves, with matched control prompts,
  prompt-variation sets, follow-up explanations and model probabilities (474,328 answers). Includes a findings report, aggregate tables, figures, prompts and a paper. No full answers or
  per-answer records. Exploratory: no pre-registration was frozen before collection.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - self-naming
  - model identity
  - output diversity
  - mode collapse
  - post-training
